#lang turmeric boguslayer
;; `#lang` takes a single base dialect and nothing else.  This used to read
;; "unknown #lang layer", back when a trailing token could name a row in a
;; curated layer registry; that axis was decommissioned, so the message names
;; what is actually wrong -- there is nowhere for a trailing token to belong.
;;
;; Same code, TUR-E0330: same failure, same class.  The one token still
;; accepted here is `stringed`, the retired layer name, which warns (TUR-W0064)
;; and is ignored for one minor line -- see tests/fixtures/lang-trailing-tokens.
(defn main [] : int 0)
